flowchart TB
  accTitle: Compare ranger, lf, and Yazi
  accDescr: Compare the three terminal file managers using the article’s categories: language and I/O, image previews, extensions, tabs, and configuration complexity. Each column presents these categories in the same order.

subgraph ranger["ranger"]
    direction TB
    rRuntime["Language and I/O<br/>Python, synchronous I/O"]
    rImages["Image previews<br/>External scripts"]
    rFeatures["Extensions and tabs<br/>Python scripts, multiple tabs"]
    rConfig["Configuration complexity<br/>Higher"]
    rRuntime ~~~ rImages ~~~ rFeatures ~~~ rConfig
  end
  subgraph lf["lf"]
    direction TB
    lRuntime["Language and speed<br/>Go, fast"]
    lImages["Image previews<br/>External scripts"]
    lFeatures["Extensions and tabs<br/>No plugin system or multiple tabs"]
    lConfig["Configuration complexity<br/>Lower"]
    lRuntime ~~~ lImages ~~~ lFeatures ~~~ lConfig
  end
  subgraph yazi["Yazi"]
    direction TB
    yRuntime["Language and I/O<br/>Rust, asynchronous I/O"]
    yImages["Image previews<br/>Built-in image protocol support"]
    yFeatures["Extensions and tabs<br/>Lua plugins, native multiple tabs"]
    yConfig["Configuration complexity<br/>Lower"]
    yRuntime ~~~ yImages ~~~ yFeatures ~~~ yConfig
  end
